ion\n84:   opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n85:   opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\n86: You can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\n87: model) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n88: \n89: Usage:\n90:   mg                              Start a session in the current project\n91:   mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n92:   mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n93:   mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n94:   mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n95: \n96: Commands:\n97:   mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),\n98:                                    set the default used by bare `\n99: \t\tmid = `, or pick\n100:                                    one via an interactive picker on a TTY\n101:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose,\n102:                                    esc/q cancel); add/rm manage your own\n103:                                    user-defined profiles (config/profiles.json)\n104:   mg setup [name] [--check]       Configure credentials for your subscriptions,\n105:                                    interactively, or report status with --check\n106:   mg theme [name]                 Show or set the global OpenCode theme\n107:                                    (OPENCODE_THEME), or pick one via an\n108:                                    interactive picker on a TTY\n109:   mg agents                       List available agents and pick one to start,\n110:                                    via an interactive picker on a TTY\n111:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose;\n112:                                    thematic alias: mg crew)\n113:   mg init [--profile <name>]      Bootstrap this project for the job workflow\n114:   mg job \"<title>\" [--type feature|fix|chore]\n115:                                    Create a job directory + branch + worktree\n116:                                    (off main)\n117:   mg jobs                         List jobs and pick one to start a session\n118:                                    in, via an interactive picker on a TTY\n119:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose); the\n120:                                    session launches in the agent appropriate\n121:                                    to the job's stage (analyst/developer/\n122:                                    reviewer)\n123:   mg done <id>                    Archive a finished job (merge + remove worktree)\n124:   mg delete <id>                  Permanently delete a job (worktree + branch, no merge)\n125:   mg prune                        Remove orphaned docker containers left behind\n126:                                    by abnormal session ends, and report how\n127:                                    many manigot containers are still running\n128:   mg diff <id> [--full|--name-only|--tig]\n129:                                    Show what a job's branch changed, three-dot\n130:                                    against the base branch (log + diff --stat\n131:                                    by default; --full for the patch, --name-only\n132:                                    for filenames, --tig to browse in tig)\n133:   mg tui                          Terminal UI for browsing jobs and firing agents\n134:   mg jdi --job/-j <id> [--profile <name>]\n135:                                    Drive a job's analyst -> developer ->\n136:                                    reviewer sequence unattended\n137:                                    (thematic alias: mg made-man)\n138:   mg host                         Run a session directly on the host — no\n139:                                    docker container; the CLI runs as-is, so\n140:                                    the agent can touch the host itself\n141:                                    (thematic alias: mg wild)\n142: mg serve                        The listener: a long-running daemon exposing\n143:                                     a read-only control API over a registry of\n144:                                     project roots (localhost default, tokenless;\n145:                                     a non-loopback bind requires a bearer token)\n146:    mg serve-token                   Generate a fresh secure token for mg serve\n147:                                     (writes MG_SERVE_TOKEN into manigot's .env)\n148: \n149:   mg -h, --help, help             Show this help\n150: \n151: A bare `\n152: \t\ttail = ` works in any project — no setup required. Project context and the\n153: job workflow (mg job/tui/jdi) additionally need a docs/ directory; see\n154: 'Per-project setup' in the manigot README to add one.\n155: `\n156: \t)\n157: \tfmt.Print(head + \"`mg`\" + mid + \"`mg`\" + tail)\n158: }\n\n(End of file - total 158 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// Package main is the single manigot host-side entry point: one `mg` binary\n// implements every command (session, profiles, setup, agents, job, jobs, done,\n// delete, init, tui, jdi, serve, host) in-process. The only bash left in the\n// project is scripts/entrypoint.sh, which runs inside the container image.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/cli\"\n\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/home\"\n)\n\n// version is the mg version. Overridden at build time with:\n//\n//\tgo build -ldflags \"-X main.version=1.2.3\"\nvar version = \"0.1.0-dev\"\n\nfunc main() {","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/src/cmd/mg/main.go","text":"// Package main is the single manigot host-side entry point: one `mg` binary\n// implements every command (sessi