{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992704501,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e195acc262b04deeb6c09517","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","limit":60,"offset":1150},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1150: \n1151: ---\n1152: \n1153: ## Listener\n1154: \n1155: `mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API over\n1156: a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a\n1157: future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. It\n1158: is the first two jobs of the control-plane sequence (read-only API, then\n1159: mutating endpoints + live run supervision with streamed logs — see the\n1160: out-of-scope list in\n1161: [`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n1162: Any frontend is a later job.\n1163: \n1164: **Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\n1165: auto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n1166: \n1167: ```bash\n1168: # <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n1169: {\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n1170: ```\n1171: \n1172: `name` is required — the URL segment the project is served under, chosen by\n1173: you (a single URL-safe path segment, unique across the registry). Nothing is\n1174: auto-derived from the directory name. Registrations are read once at startup;\n1175: changing them means editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry's `path`\n1176: must be an existing directory; a root without `docs/` is accepted and simply\n1177: lists no jobs.\n1178: \n1179: **Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\n1180: tokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\n1181: is for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n1182: `--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\n1183: no flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\n1184: must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\n1185: missing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\n1186: nginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\n1187: only safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n1188: \n1189: **API (read-only).** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\n1190: readiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\n1191: type / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n1192: `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n1193: (raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +\n1194: `session.log` tails), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick\n1195: eyeball, `?full=1` for the patch), `GET /projects/<p>/agents`, and\n1196: `GET /projects/<p>/orphans`.\n1197: \n1198: **API (mutating).** The daemon drives a job's lifecycle, not just reports on\n1199: it. Each git-mutating operation is serialized per project via\n1200: `serve.ProjectLocks`:\n1201: \n1202: - `POST /projects/<p>/jobs` — create a job (`{\"title\": \"...\", \"type\":\n1203:   \"feature|fix|chore\", \"baseBranch\": \"...\"}`) → `201` with the job row +\n1204:   branch/worktree path.\n1205: - `PUT /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/brief` — replace `brief.md` wholesale\n1206:   (an HTTP body write, no `$EDITOR`), then commit it in the job's worktree.\n1207:   The one writable job file.\n1208: - `POST /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/agents/<agent>` — launch one agent one-shot,\n1209:   detached → `202`; the caller watches the job's `session.log` (below). The\n\n(Showing lines 1150-1209 of 1272. Use offset=1210 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n---\n\n## Listener\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API over\na registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a\nfuture CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. It\nis the first two jobs of the control-plane sequence (read-only API, then\nmutating endpoints + live run supervision with streamed logs — see the\nout-of-scope list in\n[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\nAny frontend is a later job.\n\n**Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\nauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n\n```bash\n# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"\n---\n\n## Listener\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API over\na registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a\nfuture CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. It\nis the first two jobs of the control-plane sequence (read-only API, then\nmutating endpoints + live run supervision with streamed logs — see the\nout-of-scope list in\n[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\nAny frontend is a later job.\n\n**Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\nauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n\n```bash\n# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n```\n\n`name` is required — the URL segment the project is served under, chosen by\nyou (a single URL-safe path segment, unique across the registry). Nothing is\nauto-derived from the directory name. Registrations are read once at startup;\nchanging them means editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry's `path`\nmust be an existing directory; a root without `docs/` is accepted and simply\nlists no jobs.\n\n**Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\ntokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\nis for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\nno flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\nmust carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\nmissing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\nnginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\nonly safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n\n**API (read-only).** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\nreadiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\ntype / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n`GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n(raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +\n`session.log` tails), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick\neyeball, `?full=1` for the patch), `GET /projects/<p>/agents`, and\n`GET /projects/<p>/orphans`.\n\n**API (mutating).** The daemon drives a job's lifecycle, not just reports on\nit. Each git-mutating operation is serialized per project via\n`serve.ProjectLocks`:\n\n- `POST /projects/<p>/jobs` — create a job (`{\"title\": \"...\", \"type\":\n  \"feature|fix|chore\", \"baseBranch\": \"...\"}`) → `201` with the job row +\n  branch/worktree path.\n- `PUT /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/brief` — replace `brief.md` wholesale\n  (an HTTP body write, no `$EDITOR`), then commit it in the job's worktree.\n  The one writable job file.\n- `POST /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/agents/<agent>` — launch one agent one-shot,\n  detached → `202`; the caller watches the job's `session.log` (below). The","lineStart":1150,"lineEnd":1209,"totalLines":1272,"truncated":true}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1787992704490,"end":1787992704498}},"id":"prt_04cab85e7001SUFP10iUMPerdA","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","messageID":"msg_04cab7175001wXmRfPa8SGYam2"}}
