{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992723679,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_1d62d59fb8f14f90b495f359","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"serve\" /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md | head; echo ---; sed -n '80,110p' /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md"},"output":"7:opencode-go`/`--profile opencode-zen`/`--profile opencode-zen-free`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\n69:`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\n71:`<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\":\n73:operator-chosen URL segment the project is served under; no scanning;\n91:root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern — while launch-agent, launch-jdi,\n94:The token is provisioned out-of-band: `mg serve-token` generates a fresh one\n133:- `[dev command]` — start dev server\n---\nAPI is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\nhealth); job two added the mutating lifecycle (create job, edit brief, launch\none agent detached, launch mg jdi detached, done, delete, push, prune,\norphaned-worktree list + delete) and a live session-log SSE stream\n(`GET .../jobs/<j>/session-log/stream` — the network twin of the TUI's `l`\ntail, resumable via `?from=<byte offset>`), with the detached launches\nreturning 202 and the caller watching the job's session.log. The whole\nsurface is a new trust boundary: URL segments are never joined into\nfilesystem paths, credentials are never returned in any response, every\nrequest is audit-logged (never the token), and the git-mutating operations\n(create, edit-brief, done, delete, push, orphan-delete) serialize per project\nroot via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern — while launch-agent, launch-jdi,\nprune and every read endpoint deliberately do NOT take the lock, so a job\nlaunch never waits behind an unrelated merge.\nThe token is provisioned out-of-band: `mg serve-token` generates a fresh one\ninto the manigot `.env` as `MG_SERVE_TOKEN`, read once at daemon startup — the\nAPI itself never issues, creates, or returns one.\nCopying text from inside a session uses OSC 52: your terminal emulator must\nsupport it, and tmux needs `set-clipboard on` when the session runs inside\ntmux (mg forwards your terminal environment into the container and warns at\nsession start when it detects tmux would swallow the clipboard writes — see\nthe manigot README's \"Clipboard / copying from agent sessions\" section).\nOne deliberate exception in that forwarding: OpenCode sessions never see\n`TMUX`/`TMUX_PANE`, because OpenCode's TMUX-gated tmux DCS-passthrough OSC 52\nform is discarded by default tmux config (`allow-passthrough` off) — stripping\n`TMUX` makes it emit plain OSC 52, which tmux's `set-clipboard on` handles.\nThe `shot` tool (`/usr/local/bin/shot`, see the manigot README's PLAYWRIGHT\ndoc) renders a URL to a PNG + model-free render report. The developer agent\nuses it to verify rendered work; read-only agents consume the artifacts and\nnever run it.\nClaude Code respects your host terminal's own color theme automatically;\n","metadata":{"output":"7:opencode-go`/`--profile opencode-zen`/`--profile opencode-zen-free`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\n69:`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\n71:`<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\":\n73:operator-chosen URL segment the project is served under; no scanning;\n91:root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern — while launch-agent, launch-jdi,\n94:The token is provisioned out-of-band: `mg serve-token` generates a fresh one\n133:- `[dev command]` — start dev server\n---\nAPI is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\nhealth); job two added the mutating lifecycle (create job, edit brief, launch\none agent detached, launch mg jdi detached, done, delete, push, prune,\norphaned-worktree list + delete) and a live session-log SSE stream\n(`GET .../jobs/<j>/session-log/stream` — the network twin of the TUI's `l`\ntail, resumable via `?from=<byte offset>`), with the detached launches\nreturning 202 and the caller watching the job's session.log. The whole\nsurface is a new trust boundary: URL segments are never joined into\nfilesystem paths, credentials are never returned in any response, every\nrequest is audit-logged (never the token), and the git-mutating operations\n(create, edit-brief, done, delete, push, orphan-delete) serialize per project\nroot via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern — while launch-agent, launch-jdi,\nprune and every read endpoint deliberately do NOT take the lock, so a job\nlaunch never waits behind an unrelated merge.\nThe token is provisioned out-of-band: `mg serve-token` generates a fresh one\ninto the manigot `.env` as `MG_SERVE_TOKEN`, read once at daemon startup — the\nAPI itself never issues, creates, or returns one.\nCopying text from inside a session uses OSC 52: your terminal emulator must\nsupport it, and tmux needs `set-clipboard on` when the session runs inside\ntmux (mg forwards your terminal environment into the container and warns at\nsession start when it detects tmux would swallow the clipboard writes — see\nthe manigot README's \"Clipboard / copying from agent sessions\" section).\nOne deliberate exception in that forwarding: OpenCode sessions never see\n`TMUX`/`TMUX_PANE`, because OpenCode's TMUX-gated tmux DCS-passthrough OSC 52\nform is discarded by default tmux config (`allow-passthrough` off) — stripping\n`TMUX` makes it emit plain OSC 52, which tmux's `set-clipboard on` handles.\nThe `shot` tool (`/usr/local/bin/shot`, see the manigot README's PLAYWRIGHT\ndoc) renders a URL to a PNG + model-free render report. The developer agent\nuses it to verify rendered work; read-only agents consume the artifacts and\nnever run it.\nClaude Code respects your host terminal's own color theme automatically;\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"serve\" /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md | head; echo ---; sed -n '80,110p' /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787992723669,"end":1787992723674}},"id":"prt_04cabd0b7001lSrcAOOHBLw9gO","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","messageID":"msg_04cab8605001lbKETxpF5ZvmL7"}}
