{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992997572,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6c9eae6a43b84b48a47c1b86","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","limit":18,"offset":522},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n522: \n523: - **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n524:   (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n525:   `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n526:   entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n527:   under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n528:   daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means\n529:   editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry is validated at startup:\n530:   `name` non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (no `/` or `\\`, not `.` or\n531:   `..`, charset `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), unique across the registry; `path` an\n532:   existing directory. A bad entry — an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate\n533:   path, or a nonexistent directory — refuses the whole daemon to start, never\n534:   silently serving a subset; a root without `docs/` is accepted (it lists no\n535:   jobs rather than failing startup). Every handler resolves ONLY against the\n536:   registered entries, matching a URL segment by configured `name` — the\n537:   single choke point the zero-path-inputs rule builds on.\n538: - **Read-only API.** The state the TUI renders, over HTTP as JSON + raw\n539:   markdown (never ANSI): `GET /health` (version, docker image present,\n\n(Showing lines 522-539 of 848. Use offset=540 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n- **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n  (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n  `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n  entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n  under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n  daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means\n  editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry is validated at startup:\n  `name` non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (no `/` or `\\`, not `.` or\n  `..`, charset `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), unique across the registry; `path` an\n  existing directory. A bad entry — an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate\n  path, or a nonexistent directory — refuses the whole daemon to start, never\n  silently serving a subset; a root without `docs/` is accepted (it lists no\n  jobs rather than failing startup). Every handler resolves ONLY against the\n  registered entries, matching a URL segment by configured `name` — the\n  single choke point the zero-path-inputs rule builds on.\n- **Read-only API.** The state the TUI renders, over HTTP as JSON + raw\n  markdown (never ANSI): `GET /health` (version, docker image present,","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"\n- **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n  (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n  `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n  entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n  under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n  daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means\n  editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry is validated at startup:\n  `name` non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (no `/` or `\\`, not `.` or\n  `..`, charset `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), unique across the registry; `path` an\n  existing directory. A bad entry — an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate\n  path, or a nonexistent directory — refuses the whole daemon to start, never\n  silently serving a subset; a root without `docs/` is accepted (it lists no\n  jobs rather than failing startup). Every handler resolves ONLY against the\n  registered entries, matching a URL segment by configured `name` — the\n  single choke point the zero-path-inputs rule builds on.\n- **Read-only API.** The state the TUI renders, over HTTP as JSON + raw\n  markdown (never ANSI): `GET /health` (version, docker image present,","lineStart":522,"lineEnd":539,"totalLines":848,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787992997568,"end":1787992997570}},"id":"prt_04caffebe001Lljmvkfd5f6yhH","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","messageID":"msg_04caff273001k3ZPqGticMP63b"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992998532,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_f3692eb88f0d4f06a142b5a7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"mg serve \\[\\|serve-token\\|Commands$\" /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md | head; echo ---; grep -n \"mg serve\\b\" /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md | head -5; echo ---; sed -n '60,80p' /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md"},"output":"696:## Commands\n780:- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n791:- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n---\n110:- `internal/serve` — the listener daemon (`mg serve`): the project registry,\n511:`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API over\n514:first two jobs of the control-plane sequence (`mg serve` + project registry +\n780:- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n791:- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n---\nThe manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\nbranch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\nterminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\ntails the job's `session.log` — the verbose raw stream mg-jdi writes each\ninvocation's output into as it happens, distinct from the log tab's\n`run.log` event summary — live in a tmux split pane / new terminal (piped\nthrough `jq` when available on the host, falling back to a plain `tail -f`\notherwise), gated on a session.log existing for the job (created at mg-jdi\nrun start).\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\nover a registry of named project roots (an explicit config file,\n`<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\":\n[{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — `name` is the required,\noperator-chosen URL segment the project is served under; no scanning;\nchanging it means editing and restarting), so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client from localhost or a\nVPS. It binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless —\nthe machine's own user is the trust boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a\nbearer token (`--token` or `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start,\nand TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. The v1\nAPI is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\n","metadata":{"output":"696:## Commands\n780:- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n791:- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n---\n110:- `internal/serve` — the listener daemon (`mg serve`): the project registry,\n511:`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API over\n514:first two jobs of the control-plane sequence (`mg serve` + project registry +\n780:- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n791:- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n---\nThe manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\nbranch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\nterminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\ntails the job's `session.log` — the verbose raw stream mg-jdi writes each\ninvocation's output into as it happens, distinct from the log tab's\n`run.log` event summary — live in a tmux split pane / new terminal (piped\nthrough `jq` when available on the host, falling back to a plain `tail -f`\notherwise), gated on a session.log existing for the job (created at mg-jdi\nrun start).\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\nover a registry of named project roots (an explicit config file,\n`<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\":\n[{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — `name` is the required,\noperator-chosen URL segment the project is served under; no scanning;\nchanging it means editing and restarting), so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client from localhost or a\nVPS. It binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless —\nthe machine's own user is the trust boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a\nbearer token (`--token` or `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start,\nand TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. The v1\nAPI is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"mg serve \\[\\|serve-token\\|Commands$\" /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md | head; echo ---; grep -n \"mg serve\\b\" /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md | head -5; echo ---; sed -n '60,80p' /workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787992998527,"end":1787992998530}},"id":"prt_04cb00270001y6g4Q8P3Q9L869","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","messageID":"msg_04caff273001k3ZPqGticMP63b"}}
