{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787993002138,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_f75367ce166d4b5cba74d42b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","limit":18,"offset":780},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n780:   command/behavior)\n781: - `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n782:   — the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API (projects,\n783:   jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents, health, mutating lifecycle\n784:   endpoints, and a live session-log SSE stream) over a registry of project\n785:   roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to\n786:   it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. Binds\n787:   `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless — the machine's own user is the trust\n788:   boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a bearer token (`--token` or\n789:   `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start. TLS is the reverse\n790:   proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. See \"Listener / control\n791:   plane\" below.\n792: - `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n793:   write it into manigot's `.env` as `MG_SERVE_TOKEN` (32 random bytes hex via\n794:   `crypto/rand`); the daemon reads the token once at startup, so it takes\n795:   effect on the next start. The only way the token is provisioned — the API\n796:   itself never issues, creates, or returns one.\n797: \n\n(Showing lines 780-797 of 849. Use offset=798 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"  command/behavior)\n- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n  — the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API (projects,\n  jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents, health, mutating lifecycle\n  endpoints, and a live session-log SSE stream) over a registry of project\n  roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to\n  it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. Binds\n  `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless — the machine's own user is the trust\n  boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a bearer token (`--token` or\n  `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start. TLS is the reverse\n  proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. See \"Listener / control\n  plane\" below.\n- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n  write it into manigot's `.env` as `MG_SERVE_TOKEN` (32 random bytes hex via\n  `crypto/rand`); the daemon reads the token once at startup, so it takes\n  effect on the next start. The only way the token is provisioned — the API\n  itself never issues, creates, or returns one.\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"  command/behavior)\n- `mg serve [--addr <host>] [--port <n>] [--registry <path>] [--token <value>]`\n  — the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API (projects,\n  jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents, health, mutating lifecycle\n  endpoints, and a live session-log SSE stream) over a registry of project\n  roots, so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to\n  it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS. Binds\n  `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless — the machine's own user is the trust\n  boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a bearer token (`--token` or\n  `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start. TLS is the reverse\n  proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. See \"Listener / control\n  plane\" below.\n- `mg serve-token` — generate a fresh secure bearer token for `mg serve` and\n  write it into manigot's `.env` as `MG_SERVE_TOKEN` (32 random bytes hex via\n  `crypto/rand`); the daemon reads the token once at startup, so it takes\n  effect on the next start. The only way the token is provisioned — the API\n  itself never issues, creates, or returns one.\n","lineStart":780,"lineEnd":797,"totalLines":849,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787993002129,"end":1787993002135}},"id":"prt_04cb0108e0010qcd5HYFkUQw02","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","messageID":"msg_04cb0029c001iTGGUsfk4p5NjB"}}
