{"type":"text","timestamp":1787993155357,"sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","part":{"id":"prt_04cb2553f001xXbX7trYUTkt0r","messageID":"msg_04cb23cda001Pf5LuhtshDH6c0","sessionID":"ses_fb356b356ffep6vyvmzQINQBoz","type":"text","text":"Job complete. Summary of the work:\n\n**`mg serve-projects` — CLI management of `mg serve`'s registry (`config/serve.json`)**\n\n- **Store** (`src/internal/serve/registry.go`): `AddRegistryEntry`/`RemoveRegistryEntry` reuse `LoadRegistry`'s full validation on every write, so the CLI can never produce a registry the daemon would refuse to start on; a corrupt file is never silently rewritten; removing the last entry writes `[]`, not `null`.\n- **CLI** (`src/cmd/mg/serveprojects.go` + `main.go`): `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm] [--registry <path>]` — `add [path] [name]` defaults path to `$PWD` and name to the path's base name; every mutation prints the restart hint; list/add carry the daemon's missing-docs warning; `help` subcommand and `-h` wiring.\n- **Tests**: 11 store tests + 9 CLI tests; full `go test ./...`, `go vet`, `gofmt` clean, plus a manual end-to-end smoke test of the built binary (empty → add → duplicate refusal → list → rm → `{\"projects\": []}`). Note: the suite must run with the real git ahead of the session's PATH-first git shim (`PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:$PATH`), which breaks unrelated `git init`-based test setups inside the container.\n- **Docs synced**: README (table + Listener), both `AGENTS.md` copies, and `mg serve`'s usage/no-projects wording now point at `mg serve-projects`.\n- `tasks.md` and `implementation.md` filled; `verdict.md` left for the reviewer session.\n\nThe session's git mount is read-only, so the changes are left uncommitted — the host-side sweep-commit will pick them up after this session ends, as designed.","time":{"start":1787993150783,"end":1787993155351}}}
