{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787993169609,"sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_f895bf1936f343ada2e58098","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: mg serve config via cli\n2: \n3: id: spending\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: glm-5.2 (analyst pass)\n6: date: 2026-08-29\n7: \n8: ## Task breakdown\n9: \n10: TASK-1: registry store functions — `AddRegistryEntry` / `RemoveRegistryEntry`\n11: in `internal/serve`, reusing `LoadRegistry`'s validation as the single source\n12: of truth so a CLI write can never produce a file the daemon would refuse to\n13: start on (unique URL-safe name, existing directory, no duplicate paths; a\n14: corrupt file is never silently rewritten).\n15: files: src/internal/serve/registry.go, src/internal/serve/registry_store_test.go\n16: depends: none\n17: risk: low — additive functions on an existing, well-tested file format\n18: \n19: TASK-2: `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm]` CLI command in the `mg` binary,\n20: following the `mg profiles`/`mg serve-token` precedents: list the registered\n21: projects, `add [path] [name]` (path defaults to `$PWD`, name to the path's\n22: base name), `rm <name>`, `--registry` override, restart hint on every\n23: mutation, and the no-docs warning on add.\n24: files: src/cmd/mg/serveprojects.go, src/cmd/mg/serveprojects_test.go, src/cmd/mg/main.go\n25: depends: TASK-1\n26: risk: low — a new subcommand; no existing command's behavior changes\n27: \n28: TASK-3: documentation sync — `mg serve`'s usage/startup strings, the command\n29: lists in README.md, docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md, and the\n30: \"edit the file and restart\" wording in the listener sections now point at\n31: `mg serve-projects` as the primary way to change the registry.\n32: files: src/cmd/mg/serve.go, README.md, docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\n33: depends: TASK-2\n34: risk: low — text only\n\n(End of file - total 34 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: mg serve config via cli\n\nid: spending\nstatus: open\nanalyst: glm-5.2 (analyst pass)\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: registry store functions — `AddRegistryEntry` / `RemoveRegistryEntry`\nin `internal/serve`, reusing `LoadRegistry`'s validation as the single source\nof truth so a CLI write can never produce a file the daemon would refuse to\nstart on (unique URL-safe name, existing directory, no duplicate paths; a\ncorrupt file is never silently rewritten).\nfiles: src/internal/serve/registry.go, src/internal/serve/registry_store_test.go\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — additive functions on an existing, well-tested file format\n\nTASK-2: `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm]` CLI command in the `mg` binary,\nfollowing the `mg profiles`/`mg serve-token` precedents: list the registered","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: mg serve config via cli\n\nid: spending\nstatus: open\nanalyst: glm-5.2 (analyst pass)\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: registry store functions — `AddRegistryEntry` / `RemoveRegistryEntry`\nin `internal/serve`, reusing `LoadRegistry`'s validation as the single source\nof truth so a CLI write can never produce a file the daemon would refuse to\nstart on (unique URL-safe name, existing directory, no duplicate paths; a\ncorrupt file is never silently rewritten).\nfiles: src/internal/serve/registry.go, src/internal/serve/registry_store_test.go\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — additive functions on an existing, well-tested file format\n\nTASK-2: `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm]` CLI command in the `mg` binary,\nfollowing the `mg profiles`/`mg serve-token` precedents: list the registered\nprojects, `add [path] [name]` (path defaults to `$PWD`, name to the path's\nbase name), `rm <name>`, `--registry` override, restart hint on every\nmutation, and the no-docs warning on add.\nfiles: src/cmd/mg/serveprojects.go, src/cmd/mg/serveprojects_test.go, src/cmd/mg/main.go\ndepends: TASK-1\nrisk: low — a new subcommand; no existing command's behavior changes\n\nTASK-3: documentation sync — `mg serve`'s usage/startup strings, the command\nlists in README.md, docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md, and the\n\"edit the file and restart\" wording in the listener sections now point at\n`mg serve-projects` as the primary way to change the registry.\nfiles: src/cmd/mg/serve.go, README.md, docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\ndepends: TASK-2\nrisk: low — text only","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":34,"totalLines":34,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/tasks.md","time":{"start":1787993169569,"end":1787993169606}},"id":"prt_04cb29e9c001ynouqrSvDQ1KHJ","sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","messageID":"msg_04cb2952e001KxBFsu3By6MyMS"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787993169810,"sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e609a42765e74ca0a02071a1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: mg serve config via cli\n2: \n3: id: spending\n4: status: open\n5: developer: glm-5.2 (developer pass)\n6: date: 2026-08-29\n7: \n8: ## Summary\n9: \n10: Implemented `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm] [--registry <path>]` — the CLI\n11: for managing the projects registered for `mg serve` in `config/serve.json`,\n12: so nobody has to remember the JSON shape by hand.\n13: \n14: - TASK-1: PASS — store functions in `internal/serve`:\n15:   `AddRegistryEntry`/`RemoveRegistryEntry` (plus the exported\n16:   `ValidProjectName` wrapper and an internal `saveRegistry`). Both reuse\n17:   `LoadRegistry`'s full validation on every write, so the CLI can never\n18:   produce a registry the daemon would refuse to start on, and a corrupt file\n19:   is never silently rewritten. Removing the last entry writes an empty\n20:   `projects` list (never `null`, never a deleted file).\n21: - TASK-2: PASS — the `mg serve-projects` command in the `mg` binary:\n22:   list (table + the daemon's missing-docs warnings), `add [path] [name]`\n23:   (path defaults to `$PWD`, name to the path's base name; prints the\n24:   registered entry, the missing-docs warning when applicable, and the\n25:   restart hint), `rm <name>`, `--registry` override with the same default\n26:   resolution as `mg serve`, a `help` subcommand, and dispatcher + `-h` help\n27:   wiring.\n28: - TASK-3: PASS — docs synced: `mg serve`'s usage text and no-projects\n29:   warning now point at `mg serve-projects`; README.md (command table +\n30:   Listener registry paragraph), docs/AGENTS.md (Commands + \"Project\n31:   registry\" bullet), and project-template/docs/AGENTS.md (listener summary)\n32:   all document the command.\n33: \n34: ## Changes\n35: \n36: - `src/internal/serve/registry.go` — added `ValidProjectName`,\n37:   `AddRegistryEntry`, `RemoveRegistryEntry`, `saveRegistry`.\n38: - `src/internal/serve/registry_store_test.go` — new: 11 tests covering\n39:   create/append/duplicates (name and path, including a relative spelling of\n40:   an registered path)/invalid names/missing + non-directory roots/corrupt\n41:   file left untouched/remove-by-name/empty-list shape/unknown name.\n42: - `src/cmd/mg/serveprojects.go` — new: the command and its three\n43:   subcommands.\n44: - `src/cmd/mg/serveprojects_test.go` — new: 9 tests (empty list, add+list\n45:   round-trip via `serve.LoadRegistry`, the `$PWD`/basename defaults,\n46:   duplicate + missing-root errors, rm + empty-after-rm, unknown rm, usage\n47:   errors + `help`, and the no-registry-location error).\n48: - `src/cmd/mg/main.go` — dispatcher case + help entry.\n49: - `src/cmd/mg/serve.go` — usage text and no-projects warning wording.\n50: - `README.md`, `docs/AGENTS.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md` —\n51:   documentation.\n52: \n53: Verification: `go build ./...`, `go vet`, `gofmt` (touched files clean), and\n54: the full `go test ./...` suite pass (run with the real git ahead of the\n55: session's PATH-first git shim — the shim's refusal of `git init` breaks the\n56: unrelated job/ui test setups inside the container, not this change), plus a\n57: manual end-to-end smoke test of the built binary (empty list → add with\n58: default name → duplicate-path refusal → list → file contents → rm → empty\n59: `projects` list).\n60: \n61: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n62: \n63: - A running daemon still needs a restart to see registry changes (v1\n64:   design; unchanged by this job — every mutating output says so).\n65: - `rm` takes the registered name only; if a user forgets the name,\n66:   `mg serve-projects` (list) shows it. An interactive picker on a TTY could\n67:   be added later, mirroring `mg profiles`/`mg jobs`, but was not asked for.\n\n(End of file - total 67 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: mg serve config via cli\n\nid: spending\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: glm-5.2 (developer pass)\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm] [--registry <path>]` — the CLI\nfor managing the projects registered for `mg serve` in `config/serve.json`,\nso nobody has to remember the JSON shape by hand.\n\n- TASK-1: PASS — store functions in `internal/serve`:\n  `AddRegistryEntry`/`RemoveRegistryEntry` (plus the exported\n  `ValidProjectName` wrapper and an internal `saveRegistry`). Both reuse\n  `LoadRegistry`'s full validation on every write, so the CLI can never\n  produce a registry the daemon would refuse to start on, and a corrupt file\n  is never silently rewritten. Removing the last entry writes an empty\n  `projects` list (never `null`, never a deleted file).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: mg serve config via cli\n\nid: spending\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: glm-5.2 (developer pass)\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `mg serve-projects [list|add|rm] [--registry <path>]` — the CLI\nfor managing the projects registered for `mg serve` in `config/serve.json`,\nso nobody has to remember the JSON shape by hand.\n\n- TASK-1: PASS — store functions in `internal/serve`:\n  `AddRegistryEntry`/`RemoveRegistryEntry` (plus the exported\n  `ValidProjectName` wrapper and an internal `saveRegistry`). Both reuse\n  `LoadRegistry`'s full validation on every write, so the CLI can never\n  produce a registry the daemon would refuse to start on, and a corrupt file\n  is never silently rewritten. Removing the last entry writes an empty\n  `projects` list (never `null`, never a deleted file).\n- TASK-2: PASS — the `mg serve-projects` command in the `mg` binary:\n  list (table + the daemon's missing-docs warnings), `add [path] [name]`\n  (path defaults to `$PWD`, name to the path's base name; prints the\n  registered entry, the missing-docs warning when applicable, and the\n  restart hint), `rm <name>`, `--registry` override with the same default\n  resolution as `mg serve`, a `help` subcommand, and dispatcher + `-h` help\n  wiring.\n- TASK-3: PASS — docs synced: `mg serve`'s usage text and no-projects\n  warning now point at `mg serve-projects`; README.md (command table +\n  Listener registry paragraph), docs/AGENTS.md (Commands + \"Project\n  registry\" bullet), and project-template/docs/AGENTS.md (listener summary)\n  all document the command.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/internal/serve/registry.go` — added `ValidProjectName`,\n  `AddRegistryEntry`, `RemoveRegistryEntry`, `saveRegistry`.\n- `src/internal/serve/registry_store_test.go` — new: 11 tests covering\n  create/append/duplicates (name and path, including a relative spelling of\n  an registered path)/invalid names/missing + non-directory roots/corrupt\n  file left untouched/remove-by-name/empty-list shape/unknown name.\n- `src/cmd/mg/serveprojects.go` — new: the command and its three\n  subcommands.\n- `src/cmd/mg/serveprojects_test.go` — new: 9 tests (empty list, add+list\n  round-trip via `serve.LoadRegistry`, the `$PWD`/basename defaults,\n  duplicate + missing-root errors, rm + empty-after-rm, unknown rm, usage\n  errors + `help`, and the no-registry-location error).\n- `src/cmd/mg/main.go` — dispatcher case + help entry.\n- `src/cmd/mg/serve.go` — usage text and no-projects warning wording.\n- `README.md`, `docs/AGENTS.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md` —\n  documentation.\n\nVerification: `go build ./...`, `go vet`, `gofmt` (touched files clean), and\nthe full `go test ./...` suite pass (run with the real git ahead of the\nsession's PATH-first git shim — the shim's refusal of `git init` breaks the\nunrelated job/ui test setups inside the container, not this change), plus a\nmanual end-to-end smoke test of the built binary (empty list → add with\ndefault name → duplicate-path refusal → list → file contents → rm → empty\n`projects` list).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- A running daemon still needs a restart to see registry changes (v1\n  design; unchanged by this job — every mutating output says so).\n- `rm` takes the registered name only; if a user forgets the name,\n  `mg serve-projects` (list) shows it. An interactive picker on a TTY could\n  be added later, mirroring `mg profiles`/`mg jobs`, but was not asked for.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":67,"totalLines":67,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/spending_mg-serve-config-via-cli/implementation.md","time":{"start":1787993169796,"end":1787993169806}},"id":"prt_04cb29f7f001yf5VYI91rF4jRr","sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","messageID":"msg_04cb2952e001KxBFsu3By6MyMS"}}
