{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787993246150,"sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_daa0925a35ff49ecbb2ea554","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/cmd/mg/main.go","offset":80,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/workspace/src/cmd/mg/main.go</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n80: \t\thead = `mg — isolated agent environment per project (Claude Code or OpenCode, sandboxed in Docker)\n81: \n82: Profiles bundle an agent CLI with one of your subscriptions. The built-ins are:\n83:   claude-pro        Claude Code, billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription\n84:   zai               OpenCode, billed to your Z.AI Coding Plan\n85:   opencode-go       OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription\n86:   opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n87:   opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\n88: You can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\n89: model) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n90: \n91: Usage:\n92:   mg                              Start a session in the current project\n93:   mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n94:   mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n95:   mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n96:   mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n97: \n98: Commands:\n99:   mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),\n100:                                    set the default used by bare `\n101: \t\tmid = `, or pick\n102:                                    one via an interactive picker on a TTY\n103:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose,\n104:                                    esc/q cancel); add/rm manage your own\n105:                                    user-defined profiles (config/profiles.json)\n106:   mg setup [name] [--check]       Configure credentials for your subscriptions,\n107:                                    interactively, or report status with --check\n108:   mg theme [name]                 Show or set the global OpenCode theme\n109:                                    (OPENCODE_THEME), or pick one via an\n110:                                    interactive picker on a TTY\n111:   mg agents                       List available agents and pick one to start,\n112:                                    via an interactive picker on a TTY\n113:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose;\n114:                                    thematic alias: mg crew)\n115:   mg init [--profile <name>]      Bootstrap this project for the job workflow\n116:   mg job \"<title>\" [--type feature|fix|chore]\n117:                                    Create a job directory + branch + worktree\n118:                                    (off main)\n119:   mg jobs                         List jobs and pick one to start a session\n120:                                    in, via an interactive picker on a TTY\n121:                                    (type to filter, enter to choose); the\n122:                                    session launches in the agent appropriate\n123:                                    to the job's stage (analyst/developer/\n124:                                    reviewer)\n125:   mg done <id>                    Archive a finished job (merge + remove worktree)\n126:   mg delete <id>                  Permanently delete a job (worktree + branch, no merge)\n127:   mg prune                        Remove orphaned docker containers left behind\n128:                                    by abnormal session ends, and report how\n129:                                    many manigot containers are still running\n130:   mg diff <id> [--full|--name-only|--tig]\n131:                                    Show what a job's branch changed, three-dot\n132:                                    against the base branch (log + diff --stat\n133:                                    by default; --full for the patch, --name-only\n134:                                    for filenames, --tig to browse in tig)\n135:   mg tui                          Terminal UI for browsing jobs and firing agents\n136:   mg jdi --job/-j <id> [--profile <name>]\n137:                                    Drive a job's analyst -> developer ->\n138:                                    reviewer sequence unattended\n139:                                    (thematic alias: mg made-man)\n140:   mg host                         Run a session directly on the host — no\n141:                                    docker container; the CLI runs as-is, so\n142:                                    the agent can touch the host itself\n143:                                    (thematic alias: mg wild)\n144: mg serve                        The listener: a long-running daemon exposing\n145:                                      a read-only control API over a registry of\n146:                                      project roots (localhost default, tokenless;\n147:                                      a non-loopback bind requires a bearer token)\n148:   mg serve-projects [list|add|rm]  Manage the projects registered for\n149:                                      mg serve (config/serve.json): list them,\n150:                                      add a project root (path defaults to $PWD,\n151:                                      name to the path's base name), remove one\n152:                                      by name\n153:    mg serve-token                   Generate a fresh secure token for mg serve\n154:                                      (writes MG_SERVE_TOKEN into manigot's .env)\n155: \n156:   mg -h, --help, help             Show this help\n157: \n158: A bare `\n159: \t\ttail = ` works in any project — no setup required. Project context and the\n160: job workflow (mg job/tui/jdi) additionally need a docs/ directory; see\n161: 'Per-project setup' in the manigot README to add one.\n162: `\n163: \t)\n164: \tfmt.Print(head + \"`mg`\" + mid + \"`mg`\" + tail)\n165: }\n\n(End of file - total 165 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\t\thead = `mg — isolated agent environment per project (Claude Code or OpenCode, sandboxed in Docker)\n\nProfiles bundle an agent CLI with one of your subscriptions. The built-ins are:\n  claude-pro        Claude Code, billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription\n  zai               OpenCode, billed to your Z.AI Coding Plan\n  opencode-go       OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription\n  opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n  opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\nYou can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\nmodel) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n\nUsage:\n  mg                              Start a session in the current project\n  mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n  mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n  mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n  mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n\nCommands:\n  mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/src/cmd/mg/main.go","text":"\t\thead = `mg — isolated agent environment per project (Claude Code or OpenCode, sandboxed in Docker)\n\nProfiles bundle an agent CLI with one of your subscriptions. The built-ins are:\n  claude-pro        Claude Code, billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription\n  zai               OpenCode, billed to your Z.AI Coding Plan\n  opencode-go       OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription\n  opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n  opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\nYou can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\nmodel) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n\nUsage:\n  mg                              Start a session in the current project\n  mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n  mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n  mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n  mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n\nCommands:\n  mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),\n                                   set the default used by bare `\n\t\tmid = `, or pick\n                                   one via an interactive picker on a TTY\n                                   (type to filter, enter to choose,\n                                   esc/q cancel); add/rm manage your own\n                                   user-defined profiles (config/profiles.json)\n  mg setup [name] [--check]       Configure credentials for your subscriptions,\n                                   interactively, or report status with --check\n  mg theme [name]                 Show or set the global OpenCode theme\n                                   (OPENCODE_THEME), or pick one via an\n                                   interactive picker on a TTY\n  mg agents                       List available agents and pick one to start,\n                                   via an interactive picker on a TTY\n                                   (type to filter, enter to choose;\n                                   thematic alias: mg crew)\n  mg init [--profile <name>]      Bootstrap this project for the job workflow\n  mg job \"<title>\" [--type feature|fix|chore]\n                                   Create a job directory + branch + worktree\n                                   (off main)\n  mg jobs                         List jobs and pick one to start a session\n                                   in, via an interactive picker on a TTY\n                                   (type to filter, enter to choose); the\n                                   session launches in the agent appropriate\n                                   to the job's stage (analyst/developer/\n                                   reviewer)\n  mg done <id>                    Archive a finished job (merge + remove worktree)\n  mg delete <id>                  Permanently delete a job (worktree + branch, no merge)\n  mg prune                        Remove orphaned docker containers left behind\n                                   by abnormal session ends, and report how\n                                   many manigot containers are still running\n  mg diff <id> [--full|--name-only|--tig]\n                                   Show what a job's branch changed, three-dot\n                                   against the base branch (log + diff --stat\n                                   by default; --full for the patch, --name-only\n                                   for filenames, --tig to browse in tig)\n  mg tui                          Terminal UI for browsing jobs and firing agents\n  mg jdi --job/-j <id> [--profile <name>]\n                                   Drive a job's analyst -> developer ->\n                                   reviewer sequence unattended\n                                   (thematic alias: mg made-man)\n  mg host                         Run a session directly on the host — no\n                                   docker container; the CLI runs as-is, so\n                                   the agent can touch the host itself\n                                   (thematic alias: mg wild)\nmg serve                        The listener: a long-running daemon exposing\n                                     a read-only control API over a registry of\n                                     project roots (localhost default, tokenless;\n                                     a non-loopback bind requires a bearer token)\n  mg serve-projects [list|add|rm]  Manage the projects registered for\n                                     mg serve (config/serve.json): list them,\n                                     add a project root (path defaults to $PWD,\n                                     name to the path's base name), remove one\n                                     by name\n   mg serve-token                   Generate a fresh secure token for mg serve\n                                     (writes MG_SERVE_TOKEN into manigot's .env)\n\n  mg -h, --help, help             Show this help\n\nA bare `\n\t\ttail = ` works in any project — no setup required. Project context and the\njob workflow (mg job/tui/jdi) additionally need a docs/ directory; see\n'Per-project setup' in the manigot README to add one.\n`\n\t)\n\tfmt.Print(head + \"`mg`\" + mid + \"`mg`\" + tail)\n}","lineStart":80,"lineEnd":165,"totalLines":165,"truncated":false}},"title":"src/cmd/mg/main.go","time":{"start":1787993246137,"end":1787993246146}},"id":"prt_04cb3c9b6001NjwO6mrjc0Pwii","sessionID":"ses_fb34d9020ffe9TT7hHKcNCMGib","messageID":"msg_04cb3b5fc001UPKK87qy11khUa"}}
